null},{"year":2005,"returned_refugees":44,"resettlement":null,"naturalisation":null,"returned_idps":null},{"year":2006,"returned_refugees":7,"resettlement":null,"naturalisation":null,"returned_idps":null},{"year":2007,"returned_refugees":5,"resettlement":null,"naturalisation":null,"returned_idps":null},{"year":2008,"returned_refugees":6,"resettlement":null,"naturalisation":null,"returned_idps":null},{"year":2009,"returned_refugees":5,"resettlement":null,"naturalisation":null,"returned_idps":null},{"year":2011,"returned_refugees":5,"resettlement":null,"naturalisation":null,"returned_idps":null},{"year":2014,"returned_refugees":31,"resettlement":null,"naturalisation":10,"returned_idps":null},{"year":2015,"returned_refugees":7,"resettlement":null,"naturalisation":8,"returned_idps":null},{"year":2017,"returned_refugees":null,"resettlement":null,"naturalisation":5,"returned_idps":null}],"asylum_applications":{"host":[],"origin":[{"year":2015,"applied":574},{"year":2016,"applied":461},{"year":2017,"applied":459},{"year":2018,"applied":436},{"year":2019,"applied":133},{"year":2020,"applied":117},{"year":2021,"applied":225},{"year":2022,"applied":616},{"year":2023,"applied":1527},{"year":2024,"applied":1100},{"year":2025,"applied":798}]},"idmc":[{"year":2009,"total":4000},{"year":2010,"total":4000},{"year":2011,"total":4000},{"year":2012,"total":4000},{"year":2013,"total":4000},{"year":2014,"total":4000}],"footnotes":[{"year":null,"population_type":"STA","text":"In the absence of official data, the figure reported refers to stateless persons and persons with undetermined nationality identified by UNHCR partner organizations in Turkmenistan. The decrease in the reporting figure is due to naturalization in Turkmenistan and confirmation of nationality by a third country.","view":"asylum"},{"year":2021,"population_type":"STA","text":"In the absence of official data, the figure reported refers to stateless persons and persons with undetermined nationality identified by UNHCR partner organizations in Turkmenistan. The increase in the reported figure is due to the identification of new persons in stateless situations.","view":"asylum"},{"year":2022,"population_type":"STA","text":"In the absence of official data, the figure reported refers to stateless persons and persons with undetermined nationality identified by UNHCR partner organizations in Turkmenistan. The increase in the reported figure is due to the identification of new people in stateless situations.","view":"asylum"},{"year":2023,"population_type":"REF","text":"Based on reports from international organizations, UNHCR estimates that there are approximately 3,600 Afghan nationals residing in Turkmenistan who are likely in need of international protection","view":"asylum"},{"year":2023,"population_type":"STA","text":"In January 2024, the Government of Turkmenistan released for the first time ever official statistical information on stateless persons. Previously, in the absence of official data, the figure reported refers to stateless persons and persons with undetermined nationality identified by UNHCR partner organizations in Turkmenistan. Given the discrepancies between partner organizations figures and official figures as of 31 Dec 2023, UNHCR plans to continue crosschecking of partners’ database with the Turkmen authorities in 2024 in order to ensure accurate reporting for 2024. The decrease in the reported figure corresponds to those people who were naturalized or who had another nationality confirmed.","view":"asylum"},{"year":2024,"population_type":"REF","text":"Based on reports from international organizations, UNHCR estimates that there are approximately 3,400 Afghan nationals residing in Turkmenistan who are likely to be in need of international protection.","view":"asylum"},{"year":2024,"population_type":"STA","text":"In October 2024, the Government of Turkmenistan announced the resolution of all known cases of statelessness in the country, following the naturalization of a final group of 1,146 stateless people in September 2024. In February 2025, the Government reported that, as of 31 December 2024, there were no remaining stateless people in Turkmenistan. Since 2017, UNHCR has relied on figures reported by its partner organizations, as official statistical data was not made available by the authorities. In 2023, UNHCR partners launched a verification exercise to cross-check their database on stateless persons and those with undetermined nationality. This process continued in 2024 and confirmed the Government’s report. As part of the exercise, individuals were contacted to verify their current legal status. The findings showed that many had been naturalized in recent years, some had confirmed foreign nationality, and others had passed away. This verification exercise, combined with the official information provided by the Government, confirms that there are now zero officially registered stateless people in Turkmenistan. The decrease in the reported figure corresponds to those people who were naturalized or who had another nationality confirmed.","view":"asylum"},{"year":2025,"population_type":"REF","text":"At end-2025, 1 million Afghans were, for the first time, reported as other people in need of international protection in five countries. Previously, these Afghans had been reported as people in a refugee-like situation. The reclassification includes 3,200 Afghans in Turkmenistan.","view":"asylum"},{"year":2025,"population_type":"STA","text":"In October 2024, the Government of Turkmenistan announced the resolution of all known cases of statelessness in the country, following the naturalization of a final group of 1,146 stateless people in September 2024. In February 2025, the Government reported that, as of 31 December 2024, there were no remaining stateless people in Turkmenistan. Since 2017, UNHCR has relied on figures reported by its partner organizations, as official statistical data was not made available by the authorities. In 2023, UNHCR partners launched a verification exercise to cross-check their database on stateless persons and those with undetermined nationality. This process continued in 2024 and confirmed the Government’s report. As part of the exercise, individuals were contacted to verify their current legal status. The findings showed that many had been naturalized in recent years, some had confirmed foreign nationality, and others had passed away. This verification exercise, combined with the official information provided by the Government, confirms that there are now zero officially registered stateless people in Turkmenistan.","view":"asylum"}],"sources":["unhcr_countries","unhcr_population","unhcr_demographics","unhcr_idmc","unhcr_solutions","unhcr_asylum_applications","unhcr_footnotes","wpp_population","natural_earth"]}
